OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F437A1785383017
OL,3,CAnonymous tip-off line launched to
OL,4,Ctackle railway cable theft
OL,6,FTransport for Wales has launched an
OL,7,Fanonymous tip-off service, aimed at
OL,8,Ftackling cable and metal theft from
OL,9,Fthe railway network.
OL,11,FThe scheme, called TfW Protect, allows
OL,12,Fmembers of the public to report
OL,13,Finformation about suspected cable and
OL,14,Fmetal theft anonymously.
OL,16,FTransport for Wales says theft remains
OL,17,Fa significant problem, often leading
OL,18,Fto train delays and cancellations that
OL,19,Faffect passengers.
OL,1,Wj5hw}j5 ~shws                   G1/4
OL,2,W+.-'*%/"-$+,(,'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
